1
00:00:00,373 --> 00:00:04,963
(Howard:)And this is a woman who kept
a safety rail on my bed until I was 17.

2
00:00:05,127 --> 00:00:08,877
(Mrs Koothrappali:)So she has no problem
with her son being eaten by a walrus?

3
00:00:09,048 --> 00:00:10,968
(Sheldon:)That's very unlikely, Mrs. Koothrappali.

4
00:00:11,133 --> 00:00:14,633
(Sheldon:)If Raj dies, it'll be from frostbite,
gangrene, acute sunburn...

5
00:00:14,846 --> 00:00:18,636
(Sheldon:)...or being ripped to shreds
by a 1500-pound polar bear.

6
00:00:19,267 --> 00:00:22,107
(Howard:)Ma, I'm putting you on speakerphone
with Raj's parents.

7
00:00:22,270 --> 00:00:25,730
(Howard:)Can you tell them that you're okay
with me going to the Arctic?

8
00:00:25,898 --> 00:00:30,448
MRS. WOLOWITZ [ON SPEAKERPHONE]:
Arctic? I thought you said Arkansas.

9
00:00:31,779 --> 00:00:34,239
(Howard:)I didn't say that.
You never listen to me.

10
00:00:34,407 --> 00:00:35,947
(Howard's Mother:)He doesn't tell me anything.

11
00:00:36,117 --> 00:00:40,287
(Howard's Mother:)He lives a secret life
because he's ashamed.

12
00:00:41,080 --> 00:00:43,080
(Penny:)Hey, Leonard,
can I talk to you for a sec?

13
00:00:43,249 --> 00:00:47,919
(Leonard:)Sure, but let's go out here where
there's a little less yelling and guilt.

14
00:00:48,462 --> 00:00:49,752
(Leonard:)What's up?

15
00:00:49,922 --> 00:00:52,262
(Penny:)Well, I got you
a little going-away present.

16
00:00:52,425 --> 00:00:55,635
- Oh, a blanket.
- Oh, no, no. Not just a blanket.

17
00:00:55,803 --> 00:01:00,023
(Penny:)See, it has sleeves.

